[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The whiteboard view: how the canon is rendered for a person, and how to keep the render honest

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW
TITLE: The whiteboard view: how the canon is rendered for a person, and how to keep the render honest
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
STATEMENT: >>>
This is the root of the view system's own design, rendered by the same
programs that render the semantic-layer whiteboard. Nothing here is more
settled than its node says: an accepted decision is in force, an open one
is a question, a mechanism at interface-settled is designed and not yet
built.

The data model is [LINK: DEC-NARRATIVE-IS-THE-VIEW-NODE] with
[LINK: DEC-LEGEND-IS-DATA] and [LINK: DEC-TERMS-ARE-NARRATIVES]; the
programs are [LINK: MECH-VIEW-WIRELINE], [LINK: MECH-VIEW-RENDERER],
[LINK: MECH-VIEW-CHECK] and [LINK: MECH-VIEW-TASK]; the rules they answer
to are [LINK: REQ-VIEW-RENDERER-IS-CONTENT-BLIND] and
[LINK: REQ-NOTHING-DEPENDS-ON-A-NARRATIVE]; the paths that must work are
[LINK: UC-RENAME-A-TERM], [LINK: UC-RECUT-AFTER-A-RULING] and
[LINK: UC-FLIP-THE-VIEW]. The vocabulary it renders is
[LINK: DEC-NODE-FAMILIES], and the identity rule the migration rests on is
[LINK: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE].
<<<
